A||N||11||DaRkLoRD||When is a ricer not a ricer, and other ramblings..||||6||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||09-21-2000||02:00 PM||||Some recent discussions about what is "ricey" and what isn't has got me thinking..<P>on the plus side, I think a lot of the Civic body kits do look cool.. same with some cars that are dropped an inch or two. and bigger wheels usually look nice. I plan on replacing some of the badging on my GT, but nothing extreme.. just the front Fiero badge (I'm going to put on a new Pontiac symbol) I also want to powdercoat the plenum and put on a different badge, like Stimpy did. I'm also going to get a booming stereo, driving lights, ultra bright headlights, and tinted windows. except for the stereo and rebadging, every mod I plan on doing is functional for some sort of performance gain or safety (bright lights).. so, I don't think it'd be ricey.. Also, I'd have no problem with someone putting a V6 exhaust on a Duke, to improve the sound and looks.. now, that's different than putting a sticker on, saying that's the exhaust they had...<P>Now that all that stuff is out of the way...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I hate coffeecans.. they look dumb on ANY car.. same with 12" tall wings.. and wheels that are slanted outwards.. and cars that are lowered so much they scrape the ground.. and cars with stickers for parts they don't have.. and let's not forget those wonderful fake cross-drilled rotors...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I think useless modifications are "ricey", especially if they try to fool people into thinking the car is better than it is.. (such as a VTEC sticker on a car without a VTEC engine..) but if a person wants to have a bright orange car with purple accents... I wouldn't call it ricey. you wouldn't catch me dead ever doing anything like that to *my* car... but I wouldn't call it rice. As soon as the person slapped on a coffeecan, *then* it'd be rice.. unless it had an engine big enough to warrant a true 3" or larger exhaust system... but big tips are just useless IMHO.<P>sorry if I unintentionally offended anyone, I just wanted to share some thoughts on what what I think "rice" is, and hopefully start a discussion so everyone share ideas and we could decide on what generally classifies a car as "rice".. maybe it might help avoid offending some people in the future, if they do an asthetic mod and someone calls it "ricey"..<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 09-21-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||whamel||09-21-2000||02:42 PM||||Seems to some people 'Ricer' is the guy who won the race.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RiceCooker||09-21-2000||03:17 PM||||Elaborate.||||reg||1
Z||000003||whamel||09-21-2000||03:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, lucidatypewriter">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RiceCooker:<BR><B>Elaborate.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Here's one, I'm out (a while back) racing this guy at a light - smoked him pretty good and we hit the next light together.  He rolls down his windows and calls me a 'ricer'.<BR>I was driving a solid black car, no extra stickers (in fact, the only stickers on the car were the little R/T below the passenger taillight), All mods were 'performance oriented' and hidden under hood, my exhaust was modified - but you wouldn't know it from looking, and I didn't initiate the race - he did.  And I certainly didn't say anything to him at all.  WTF?  How's that make ME a 'ricer'?<BR>What was the other guy driving?  A pretty cool older Mustang GT.  Good shape, nice paint job, good sounding engine - very nice.<BR>Funny how many times I hear my Fiero GT is 'rice' too out on the street.  I expect to hear POS, but not 'rice'.<BR>Wade<BR>P.S. and in case you're wondering - I had NO body mods on that car at all, everything externally was stock as Dodge blessed it out the door.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||RiceCooker||09-21-2000||04:01 PM||||Sounds to me like the mustang guy had his head up his a$$ and was sore loser.<BR>As for anyone else calling your fiero ricey....<P>??????????????????<P>Maybe some people just don't know how to take a loss or maybe it's because rice is becoming a more and more popular term and not that many people know what it actually means||||reg||1
Z||000005||whamel||09-21-2000||04:08 PM||||The Mustang guy always had his head up his A$$.  I beat him in my T-type Buick as well and that never should have happened.  Heck, I probably could beat him in my truck.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I still can't figure out the 'rice fiero' thing, but I guess it's just because I seem to come from the 'Land of the V8' or something.  Some of these guys where I live just can't believe the fact that a 4 cylinder straight from the factory can beat a V8.  Go figure.<P>Hey - if I earn a 'Rice Citation' then at least tell me why!  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||HugGRRRFiero||09-21-2000||04:21 PM||||Gota Agree with Cooker...  I would have told the guy in the Mustang, "Ricer?       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">, Ok, well whatever you want to call it, it still beat you."       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>He's probably got a real bad complex going. Being beat by a Buicks, Camaros, now Fieros.  I know thats gota be wearing on his self esteem pretty good.<p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 09-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||whamel||09-21-2000||08:04 PM||||You know - I was reading somewhere (I think it was riceboy.com) about a guy with a real Type-R Acura who went to a show and nobody believed that it was actually a Type-R.  Kept calling him a ricer and he had to pull out the sticker to prove it.  That's kind of sad.  <BR>I don't care what anybody says - I think the Type-R is a nice car and deserves a lot of respect.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Greg Piet||09-21-2000||09:24 PM||||Speaking of a real type R.... At the last autocross I went to there was a right hand drive type R there...<BR>It was fast, but unfortunately the driver was not skilled enough to drive it correctly...  That car did get a lot of looks!  Especially from the riceboys that usually come out to watch the "big boys" drive.<P>BTW:  "big boys" does not correspond to engine displacement, but actual ability to drive.  There are a few riceboys that do race, but normally they get spanked pretty hard. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Black88GT||09-21-2000||10:59 PM||||Man, I hate rice fiero's.  They give all fiero's and fiero onwers a bad name.  The only one I have seen personally was an '88 coupe, ugly green with stickers, and a ricer exhaust tip.  I saw him a bunch and then I decided to talk to him.  He knew nothing about Fiero's except that he always got spanked by fellow ricers.  I was about to steal his car to save face for other fiero owners.  No wonder the ricers around here have no respect for Fiero's!!  Another very good example of fiero rice can be found at<BR> <A HREF="http://www.midwestmodifieds.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.midwestmodifieds.com/</A> <P>click on "Club members" and click on the 6th name from the top in the left hand column (don't want to mention any names).  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Greg Piet||09-22-2000||03:37 AM||||Well I must admit that Riced Fiero has a few things that I would like...   namely I could USE one of those seats and a harness.  YES I can USE it!   In those little autocross races I get thrown around in the cockpit and would like to be able to focus more on driving than on keeping my butt planted in the seat.<P>I got a real kick out of the NOS pressure gauge, although I did nto see NOS as an upgrade listed...  I somehow doubt that he forgot to list NOS sice he mentioned such things as "white gauges", and plug wires.<P>Now I have a number of those things but I think of myself as pretty far from rice! Namely MSD, K+N, short shifter, and I have a fire extinguisher in the trunk.<P>With all those goodies I just HOPE he knows how to use the added performance otherwise he has way too much $$$.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||09-22-2000||06:49 PM||||I have a fire extinguisher too, in the trunk.  I don't have it mounted to the dash.  That looks really tacky.  The worst part about the car is the pale yellow accents with maroon paint and STOCK wheels.  If it was black with yellow accents and 17" wheels it might be a little different.  The funny thing is, he says its "hennesey viper yellow", I have seen the hennesey viper yellow and that is definitely NOT it!!<P>||||reg||1
